---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero2 from '~/components/widgets/Hero2.astro';
import TextSplit from '~/components/widgets/TextSplit.astro';
import CTABanner from '~/components/widgets/CTABanner.astro';
import Text from '~/components/ui/Text.astro';
import Button from '~/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { getSanityAboutImages } from '~/lib/content/sanity';

const aboutImages = await getSanityAboutImages();

const metadata = {
  title: 'About El Ranchero | Our Story & Local Sourcing on Oahu',
  description:
    'Learn about El Ranchero. Founded in Kailua in 2006, we serve fresh, locally sourced food across six Oahu locations. Read our story.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {/* ── Page hero ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <Hero2
    variant="split-dark"
    overlapHeader={false}
    title="About El Ranchero"
    content="Kailua-born since 2006. Six locations across Oahu. Twenty years of fresh, locally sourced food made with ingredients you can trust."
    image={aboutImages.hero}
    imageFit="contain"
    actions={[
      { variant: 'primary', text: 'View Menu', href: '/menu' },
      { variant: 'ghost-dark', text: 'Find a Location', href: '/locations' },
    ]}
  />

  {/* ── 1. Our Mission ────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit heading="Our Mission">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
        <Text variant="body-lg" color="default" class="italic">
          "El Ranchero was established to serve fresh, locally grown food of the highest quality at affordable prices.
          We remain dedicated to supporting local farmers and fishermen while providing our customers with fresh and
          delicious ingredients."
        </Text>
      </blockquote>
      <Text variant="body" color="muted">
        That commitment has guided every decision we have made since May 2006 — from the produce we source to the
        dressings we make from scratch every morning.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 2. Our Story ──────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit
    heading="Our Story"
    withImage
    image={aboutImages.story}
    imageAspect="4 / 5"
    class="bg-card"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        El Ranchero opened its first location at Kailua Shopping Center in May 2006. From day one, the goal was
        straightforward: give the community a place to eat food that is genuinely good for you, made with ingredients
        you can trust, at prices that make that easy to do every day.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Twenty years later, that original promise still runs the kitchen. What started as a single neighborhood spot has
        grown into six locations across Oahu — each one serving the same scratch-made dressings, the same never-frozen
        local ahi, and the same produce sourced as close to home as possible.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        In 2024, the Star Advertisers Peoples Choice Awards named us <strong>First Place, Hawaiis Best</strong>.
        We are proud of it — and more proud that it came from the community we have been serving since the beginning.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="muted" class="text-sm italic">
        {/* TODO: Founder story — additional details coming soon */}
        Founder story coming soon.
      </Text>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 3. Sustainability — image left / text right ──────────── */}
  <TextSplit
    heading="Sustainability"
    withImage
    image={aboutImages.sustainability}
    imageReverse
    imageAspect="4 / 3"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        The most straightforward thing we do for sustainability is buy local — on a standing weekly order, not as a
        trend. Hauula tomatoes come in every week from a single Oahu farm. Our produce comes from island growers
        wherever the season and supply hold up. The ahi on your plate was never frozen and came from Hawaii waters.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Keeping the supply chain short means less transport, less cold-chain energy, and money that stays in the state.
        It also means the food is fresher when it reaches your bowl.
      </Text>
      {/* TODO: Packaging — details to be confirmed and added here */}
      <Text variant="body" color="muted" class="text-sm italic"> Packaging details coming soon. </Text>
      <div>
        <Button variant="primary" text="See Our Ingredients" href="/ingredients" hideNote={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 4. Our Vendors — text left / image right ─────────── */}
  <TextSplit
    heading="Our Vendors"
    withImage
    image={aboutImages.vendors}
    imageAspect="4 / 3"
    class="bg-section-grey"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        Every delivery of local ahi arrives with a lot number and the name of the catch vessel on the paperwork. We know
        where the fish came from. That traceability is non-negotiable.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Our other key suppliers — produce, proteins, and pantry — are all confirmed and operating on standing orders.
        We are not publishing names yet, but the sourcing page covers what is on your plate and where it comes from.
      </Text>
      <div>
        <Button variant="primary" text="See Our Ingredients" href="/ingredients" hideNote={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Find a Location CTA ───────────────────────────────── */}
  <CTABanner
    title="Find a Location"
    subtitle="Six neighborhood restaurants across Oahu. Come see us."
    ctaText="Find a Location"
    ctaHref="/locations"
  />
</PageLayout>
